  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Researchers are trying to count the number of penguins in a colony. One day they catch 20 penguins, tag their legs, and then set them free. The next day they randomly catch 48 penguins, of which 4 have tagged legs. How many penguins do you estimate are in the colony?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "About 240 penguins.\n\nScale the sample by $20\\div4=5$ to match the total number tagged.",
      "worked": "The sample contains 4 tagged penguins out of 48. The colony contains 20 tagged penguins, so scale both quantities by $20\\div4=5$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Estimated colony population}&=48\\times\\frac{20}{4}\\\\\\text{Estimated colony population}&=240\\end{align*}$$\n\nThere are approximately 240 penguins in the colony.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
